WEBVTT

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:08.940
This man was once
the king's closest friend.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:13.110
After the king's death,
he sometimes guided me like a brother

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.280
and sustained this kingdom.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:17.450
Even so...

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:24.580
...those who sell their souls
to demons are bound for hell.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.290
What's going on?!

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:27.750
Listen well!

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:30.920
The queen dowager's
family and Lord Hastings

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:33.970
attempted to assassinate
the Duke of Gloucester!

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:36.510
Lord Stanley.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:38.510
You backed the wrong horse.

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:43.930
Did you all see that?!

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:48.360
Lord Hastings not only spread baseless
slanders against the Duke of Gloucester,

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:51.440
but even attempted to murder
the duke by sorcery!

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:52.900
Yet have not fear!

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.950
He was executed before our eyes
and his schemes forestalled!

00:00:56.950 --> 00:01:01.040
The Lord God could see the justice
in the Duke of Gloucester's heart!

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:06.670
Our Lord Protector! Please have mercy!

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:12.090
I swear to turn over a new leaf
and serve you body and soul!

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.800
Very well.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:17.550
Hear me: it is not yet too late.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:21.310
If we can join hands for England's sake,

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:23.770
I shall call you

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:26.560
my brothers.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:27.940
I'm so close.

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:31.400
Soon, my hands will be able to grasp

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:32.520
the light!

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:38.700
York of the white rose.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:41.370
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:47.750
These royal houses with roses for
their crests battled for the throne.

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:52.420
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:31.390
Queen Dowager Elizabeth.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:33.060
What a shame.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:36.270
All of your schemes have fallen flat.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:37.690
Buckingham!

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:44.530
You had cause to want the
Duke of Gloucester dead at any cost.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:51.790
He is the true heir to the throne,
more legitimate than your sons.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:53.620
What?! How dare you!

00:03:53.620 --> 00:04:00.590
Catesby, speak the dreadful truth
you once heard on the field of battle.

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:06.600
What I am about to say is supported
by a wealth of testimony.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.810
I swear to the Lord Our God
that I speak the truth.

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:13.810
Our former king, Edward IV,

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:19.070
was already married to another woman
before he met Elizabeth Woodville.

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:25.530
Elizabeth Woodville is
not the king's lawful wife.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:29.910
Therefore, her son Edward
is not a legitimate king.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:32.330
This is a grievous mistake!

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:36.710
A lowly weed has put down
roots in the sacred palace!

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:38.130
But gentlemen!

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:42.840
Fortunately, the prince does not yet
wear a golden crown upon his brow!

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:47.550
We can still correct our error!

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:50.100
God is watching over us!

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:57.520
Enact justice.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:01.190
Take both brothers away!

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:03.490
To the Tower of London
with this false king!

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:04.740
S-Stop it!

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:07.410
Take your filthy hands off me!

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:09.160
I am king!

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:10.830
Damn that demon!

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:16.000
Richard! You'll pay for this!

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:29.220
The time has come at last.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:32.680
How you and I have waited for this moment.

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:34.600
"You and I"...?

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:41.610
Once the time comes, we need
no longer reaffirm our pact.

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:46.860
The king's body belongs to the kingdom.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.660
Naturally.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:52.030
Are you worried about what Jane said?

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:55.330
But do you truly understand yourself?

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:59.460
Rest easy. That's not possible.

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:03.840
Do you have proof of that,
or do you merely wish to believe it?

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:07.130
The terrible nights will return,

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:09.840
even though I've already known warmth.

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:12.720
Richard?

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:14.510
It's for the crown.

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:17.520
Our pact is merely a ritual to that end.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:21.400
Isn't that right, Richard?
If you have the makings of a king...

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:23.820
I...

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:27.360
...can't sleep without you.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:34.120
Forget that.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:37.870
How you toy with my resolve.

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:40.500
Coupling isn't the extent of our pact.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:42.250
Tell me your desire.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:49.630
Just be at my side.

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:54.680
Until the darkness burns
away in the morning sunlight.

00:06:56.220 --> 00:07:00.940
Have you heard?! Edward V and his brother
were taken to the Tower of London!

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:02.900
What on earth is going on?!

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:05.480
If that's true,
the next heir to the throne

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:07.070
can only be him!

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:13.240
What's wrong? Doesn't this feel real?

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:15.490
When I thought I held it,

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:20.160
light has always turned
to curses in my hands.

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:22.170
This time, it's real.

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:25.710
No one remains between us and the throne.

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:28.550
All the briars have been cleared away.

00:07:28.550 --> 00:07:30.800
You need only wish.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:34.340
Now, all shall be as you desire.

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:36.720
Where is the Duke of Gloucester?

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:39.470
Praying at the Tower of London, I hear.

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:42.560
Pressing on his wounds
and praying, they say.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:48.110
Fools! They'll all act out
his script if nothing is done.

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:54.110
Let me tell you what he has already done!

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:56.700
He killed his friends,
killed his brothers,

00:07:56.700 --> 00:08:00.540
and now he's praying in feigned innocence

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:02.660
in that place!

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:06.170
Henry VI died here.

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:07.630
I killed him.

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:11.760
He called me a demon.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:16.010
Richard is without compassion, for he

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:19.850
was not fashioned in God's image!

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:23.980
Now you mention it, there were
rumors about his true self.

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:26.860
I heard them, too. About what he really is.

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:30.980
Yeah! Everyone was saying that Richard,
Duke of Gloucester is a demon!

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:33.530
You must not crown a demon king!

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:39.620
If a demon takes the throne, England
will be plunged into the depths of ruin!

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:42.200
Your Grace! A mob surrounds the Tower!

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.460
Demon!

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:44.750
Get out, demon!

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:47.460
Don't crown the demon!

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:48.290
Your Grace...

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:52.590
They call for me, and I shall answer.

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:54.670
Are you ready, Buckingham?

00:08:54.670 --> 00:08:58.430
The script is complete. Now, act it.

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:01.720
The curses of the dead
only trouble humans.

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:06.350
Demons merely do as they wish.

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:08.730
Listen. This is a ruse.

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:11.320
No matter how I beg you,

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:14.570
simply spurn my demands
like a pure maiden.

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:18.620
It's your cue, Richard.
Your role is "God."

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:20.330
Yes.

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:24.450
I'll give a performance of holiness
that will hoodwink God himself.

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:34.170
Demon, you say?! Nonsense!

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:38.050
This is the legitimate
scion of the Plantagenets,

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:40.140
the renowned Duke of Gloucester!

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:42.390
The new King of England!

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:46.020
What insolence! You may play the saint,

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:49.230
but you can't hide
the rot within, usurper!

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:51.400
Buckingham, face me.

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:59.410
How dare you?! I am not the king!

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:03.410
True, I have long desired the crown.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:08.000
But only to offer to Prince Edward,
my beloved brother's heir!

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.630
Your Majesty is mistaken!

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:13.300
That boy is no prince!

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:15.590
You all must know as well!

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:20.550
Lustful Edward IV neglected war
and even despoiled his subjects' wives!

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:23.180
At last, he conceived
those boys in bigamy!

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:26.770
Nonsense! Don't let the demon's
tawdry act deceive you!

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:31.900
You may be my friend,
but I'll forgive no more such slights!

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:36.400
If speaking the truth is a crime,
then I await my punishment.

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:42.320
But you have never yet killed
anyone who spoke the truth.

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:46.870
Your love for your brother's
children is what drives you.

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:52.250
You wish to give them the exalted
station and happiness of kingship!

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:55.500
I have only one desire:

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:59.550
A light to shine on this dark world.

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:06.350
On bloody mornings,
troubled days, and lonely nights.

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:11.560
A light to illuminate our proper path.

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:14.440
I want someone to be that light.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:16.690
Not "someone."

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:22.700
You. You will become the light
that shines on this world.

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:28.910
The chaos of a child king's reign
begets suffering for the people.

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:33.670
None know the pains of such
an age better than you.

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:39.050
Of course. Strife will break out
around a powerless king.

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:41.590
I don't want to see that chaos again.

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:43.800
I lost my son in the wars.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:45.850
Yes, and I my father.

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:48.890
My father...

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:52.100
My father was everything to me.

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:56.310
All lies! Even those tears!

00:11:56.310 --> 00:11:58.940
It doesn't look that way to me.

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:05.070
I felt a special bond between us.

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:06.990
Preserve my name.

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:08.740
Yes, Father.

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:13.250
Duke of Gloucester!

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:16.460
If you will not listen
to all my entreaties,

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:20.050
I will be forced to claim the throne
through another bloodline!

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:22.720
--Stop!
--Duke of Gloucester, stop the wars!

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:24.550
Please! Please, Your Grace!

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:25.720
All of you join in!

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:27.350
Hear our pleas!

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:29.600
Grant our wish, Duke of Gloucester!

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:30.970
--King!
--King!

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:31.810
King!

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:32.930
Save us!

00:12:32.930 --> 00:12:34.230
Defend us!

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:35.690
O Lord, please!

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:36.560
Wait!

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:40.690
I will not allow England to fall to ruin,

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:44.610
even if I must forsake my
soul's justice to prevent it.

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:47.740
Buckingham, people of London,

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:51.160
I will become king

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:54.500
and shoulder the weight of destiny!

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:55.540
O Lord!

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:57.170
Praise be to God!

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:02.710
Richard, named for his father,
shall become the light of this world!

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:14.060
God save our new king!

00:13:16.640 --> 00:13:20.020
What's going on? Some kind of festival?

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:20.980
Yes.

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:23.490
The new king's coronation.

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:26.070
Edward V's coronation?!

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:28.620
Then Richard's reign is over!

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:32.330
Yes, that means we'll soon be free.

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:34.410
O little robin, bearer of good news!

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:37.210
Let's toast our new king together!

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:38.960
To our king!

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:48.590
The day I was given life,
a terrible storm laid trees low.

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:52.970
Owls screeched and crows
croaked in the night

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:58.350
to herald the coming
of an age of misfortune.

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:10.820
Tell me, Father, why does
everyone do what the king says?

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:15.080
Because God chose the king.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:18.120
If God chose me...

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:21.840
If I became king,
would I never be sad again?

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:26.050
Of course not.
You would have your every wish.

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:27.550
Listen, Richard.

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:34.220
Within that crown--
that golden circlet--lies paradise.

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:36.470
Let me prophecy, Richard.

00:14:36.470 --> 00:14:40.690
One day, a host of the elderly,
of widows, of orphans

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:46.360
will bless you even as they lament
the loved ones they have lost.

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:48.570
Because God...

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:55.620
Because God has chosen this bloody demon.

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:59.710
Now I bless you with your royal title!

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:06.250
Your Majesty, Richard III,
King of England!

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:09.090
May God's blessing be upon you!

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:16.600
May the Lord God redeem us as well.

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:22.060
Make way for His Majesty!

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:24.520
Allow me to congratulate Your Majesty!

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:28.190
Bless His Majesty, King Richard III!

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:31.240
Does it truly blind people this much?

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:36.330
They heap praises upon
the crown's radiance,

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:41.160
never noticing the demon's horns
hidden by its halo of light.

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:48.340
The wounds of civil strife have healed,
and peace breathes once more!

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:53.470
I humbly pray to God that
this peace may be eternal.

00:15:56.180 --> 00:15:59.270
This is impressive for
an impromptu celebration.

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:03.940
Of course it is. It was originally
meant for Edward V.

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:07.820
Now, please turn your attention
to our next entertainment!

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:13.320
Almighty God! I beg your permission
to create a heaven here!

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:16.910
I am God, the King of Kings!

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:21.790
O Lord! Eternal loyalty to you alone!

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:26.170
I thought this play was
chosen to please Edward.

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:28.040
Why this subject?

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:29.670
Listen well, angels!

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:33.300
Touch not my throne while I am gone!

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:35.840
I know what God said,

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:41.600
but if I sat on that throne,
might I gain power equal to His?

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:45.850
My radiance has earned me
a rank second only to Him.

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:50.020
My name is Lucifer!

00:16:50.020 --> 00:16:54.240
Your light is many times brighter
and more beautiful than God's!

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:57.030
You should sit upon His throne at once!

00:16:57.030 --> 00:17:00.450
All Heaven belongs to you and me!

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:04.040
Behold! The power of God is now mine!

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:07.420
Kneel before your true sovereign!

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:09.590
This is clearly...

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:12.210
Lèse-majesté! Make them cease at once!

00:17:12.210 --> 00:17:14.590
Northumberland, leave them.

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:16.430
But...

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:18.260
Show us the rest.

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:19.800
What folly!

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:23.680
Fall into Hell and be bound there forever!

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:26.600
God loves me no more!

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:29.770
I envy humans, who have God's love!

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:34.820
Yes, this certainly is Richard.

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:36.400
Or at least it <i>was</i>.

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:41.870
I shall reward you
for that fine diversion.

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:45.160
Catesby, show them the finest hospitality.

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:49.080
Actor, you are invited
to tomorrow's banquet.

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:51.790
I'll show you the sequel to your play.

00:17:51.790 --> 00:17:55.760
But in Richard's world this time.

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:59.140
Change everything about
tomorrow's banquet.

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:02.220
Make sure no one could
mistake it for Edward's.

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:08.020
My banquet will show them
that Richard's new age has come!

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:09.650
Edward.

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:12.570
Mother. Father.

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:16.490
I wanted to bid you goodnight.

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:18.820
Your Royal Highness.

00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:24.040
Pardon me; I've never had the chance
to properly introduce myself before.

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:29.290
I am delighted to see that you
have grown into a splendid youth.

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:33.090
Th-Thank you very much,
Duke of Buckingham.

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:39.010
Buckingham, may I have a moment?
I wish to speak with you.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:44.180
I'll sleep with Anne tonight.

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:50.190
I'm king, and spending nights
with the queen is a king's duty.

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:53.730
Naturally.

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:55.400
Do you mind?

00:18:55.400 --> 00:18:59.070
Our pact has been fulfilled.

00:18:59.070 --> 00:19:01.660
Become a perfect king.

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:03.780
That is my wish.

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:10.410
The royal apartments.

00:19:10.410 --> 00:19:11.710
Will you drink?

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:15.460
Yes.

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:16.300
What?

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:20.220
Well, it's strange, but I'm nervous.

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:23.640
I've never been in your room before.

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:26.260
Although we've been married so long.

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:27.680
Get used to it.

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:29.600
As should you.

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:33.520
If only we had always been so close,

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:36.610
like I dreamed of back then.

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:39.690
Maybe for us, this is...

00:19:39.690 --> 00:19:42.990
It's all too late.

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:45.620
The queen is the king's other half.

00:19:47.410 --> 00:19:49.750
We must support each other to survive.

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:57.500
Richard, are you hurt?

00:20:01.920 --> 00:20:03.180
Richard?

00:20:05.050 --> 00:20:10.180
Sorry. I'm tired tonight,
and there's another feast tomorrow.

00:20:10.180 --> 00:20:11.730
It's fine.

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:14.850
Am I drunk on my newfound light?

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:21.070
Without the crown's radiance to hide in,
I'm only a demon--only Richard.

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:24.360
Am I more frightened
now that I've obtained it?

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:28.990
Now that I know what it's like
to be "permitted" warmth?

00:20:30.330 --> 00:20:32.660
In this hazy world,

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:38.290
the path my soul showed me
was always clear and bright.

00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:43.090
I created a king--
an ideal king--and yet...

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:49.890
Are my feelings for Richard...?

00:20:55.390 --> 00:20:58.360
I was scared stiff tonight.

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:01.400
I always said it was a bad idea.

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:04.820
Thank goodness King Richard
was the forgiving sort.

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:05.860
Yeah,

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:09.870
but you never know when
a king will change his mind.

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:12.910
Let's make ourselves scarce
before we end up hanged for--

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:19.710
I can smile and murder while I smile,

00:21:19.710 --> 00:21:23.210
and cry, "Content!" to that
which grieves my heart,

00:21:23.210 --> 00:21:26.510
and wet my face with artificial tears.

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:29.140
I'll deceive more slyly than Ulysses could

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:32.390
and slay more gazers than the basilisk.

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:37.730
Can I do this...

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:42.780
...and cannot get...

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:45.400
...a crown?
